# Deploy

GitHub is version control only. Never GitHub Pages, GitHub Actions
deploy, `actions/deploy-pages`, `withastro/action`, or
`cloudflare/wrangler-action`. Do not add `.github/workflows/` that ships
the site.

**CI/CD is Cloudflare Workers Builds.** That is the one pipeline. If
someone asks to set up CI/CD or add a pipeline, load
`.cursor/skills/workers-builds-ci/`. Do not invent another.

Talk in simple words. Roman is not a professional developer. If a rule
or plugin skill fights this path, say so, follow this path, and fix the
stale text. Do not ask him to pick between two setups.

**Published** = a visitor can see the change at https://rtikhonov.com

Production is Cloudflare Worker `rtikhonov`. The live app is the
**repository root** (`wrangler.jsonc` here). Edit `src/`. Open PRs into
`main`.

## Everyday ship

1. Small change (typo, blog note, tiny copy): `npm run check` if the
   tree is dirty, then merge.
2. Large change (new page, new UI): look first with
   `.cursor/skills/preview-site/`. Optional web link = branch preview
   from Builds. Then merge.
3. Cloudflare Workers Builds deploys (`npm run build`, then
   `npx wrangler deploy`). The Worker is already connected to this repo.
4. Cache-bust curl https://rtikhonov.com and confirm the new string

Dashboard settings live in `docs/deploy.md`. Do not invent a hosting-branch
checkout. There is no second Astro app.

## Emergency only

If Builds is not connected or failed:

```bash
npx wrangler whoami
npm run deploy
```

Cloud Agents need `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` in Cursor environment secrets
with **Workers Scripts Edit**. If `whoami` works but deploy returns 403 /
code 10000, the token is too weak — ask the owner to fix it. Do not run
`wrangler login` and wait on a localhost OAuth callback. Do not use hand
deploy to “test CI.”

## Do not

- Fetch `cursor/cloudflare-workers-hosting` or `cd rtikhonov.com/`
- Treat a green GitHub check as published (check the live URL)
- TodoWrite for a clean-tree ship
- Re-run `check:docs` / `astro build` before `npm run deploy` when the tree is clean
- Hard-require `/Users/rtikhonov/Desktop/...`
- Add `test.rtikhonov.com` unless the owner asks for that as its own task
